Wait, but `types.Graph` is the exported Graph type. Can I chain `.narrow` on it? Yes, the exported types are Type instances, so `.narrow` is available.

Let me write the narrow function. The narrow predicate receives the validated Graph value (with shape already validated). So `g.rootId`, `g.nodes` are available. Each node has `id`, `label`, `edges` (array of full Node objects). 

Constraints:
1. All nodes[*].id unique.
2. For every node n and every edge e in n.edges, e.id must exist in nodes ids.
3. rootId exists in nodes ids.

Let me write:
```ts
const Graph = types.Graph.narrow((g, ctx) => {
  const ids = new Set<number>();
  for (const node of g.nodes) {
    if (ids.has(node.id)) {
      return ctx.mustBe(`unique node ids (duplicate id ${node.id})`);
    }
    ids.add(node.id);
  }
  // rootId exists
  if (!ids.has(g.rootId)) {
    return ctx.mustBe(`rootId ${g.rootId} to exist in nodes`);
  }
  // edge target existence
  for (const node of g.nodes) {
    for (const edge of node.edges) {
      if (!ids.has(edge.id)) {
        return ctx.mustBe(`edge target id ${edge.id} to exist in nodes`);
      }
    }
  }
  return true;
});
```

